Subject: [PATCH 5/6] feat: frontend English mode when input has no candidates

For table schemas like wubi without sentence input, an invalid code leaves
the engine with no candidates. When auto_english/enabled is on, the frontend
takes over at that point: it seeds a buffer from the raw input, clears the
Rime composition, and accumulates further ASCII (letters, digits, symbols,
space) on its own, committing only on Return (reusing pangu spacing). This
sidesteps the engine re-matching Chinese after a space, which Lua can't avoid.

- Left/Right arrows move the caret inside the buffer; Backspace edits it;
  Escape discards; other keys flush the buffer then pass through.
- Preedit display follows style/inline_preedit (inline marked text or the
  floating panel), so it shows where the user expects.
- Config switch auto_english/enabled (default off), read per schema like the
  pangu/smart-space switches.
